                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "VADs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22bbce3a-25a3-3daa-81f7-4919e2e7e43b",
                        "entry_id": "64c824bd-d929-31a1-813c-5dadba249cc7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of Voluntary Aid Detachment: a women′s first-aid organisation active during World War I and World War II, or a member of this detachment; also V.A.D."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "historical",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2bc738c-bc17-4d51-9abe-655db88f3ba2",
                                "sense_id": "22bbce3a-25a3-3daa-81f7-4919e2e7e43b",
                                "text": "A young girl in V.A.D. uniform ran lightly across the lawn."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f65d7b5c-2359-4f4f-a7f0-c0c278be6ce9",
                                "sense_id": "22bbce3a-25a3-3daa-81f7-4919e2e7e43b",
                                "text": "‘You've not been caught in bed with a V.A.D.?’ Tietjens asked."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37b06d84-721f-44ba-854c-a3cd4fd51337",
                                "sense_id": "22bbce3a-25a3-3daa-81f7-4919e2e7e43b",
                                "text": "‘A nurse is like a doctor. It takes a long time to be. A VAD is a short cut.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98c7f07e-8716-4f1b-b430-b9671c90d1f7",
                                "sense_id": "22bbce3a-25a3-3daa-81f7-4919e2e7e43b",
                                "text": "If Mollie Skinner was ever technically a member of a Voluntary Aid Detachment in India she would have been an unusually experienced and well-qualified one. VADs were more frequently lady amateurs[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "923d60be-479d-4b51-ad67-4992f90926ec",
                                "sense_id": "22bbce3a-25a3-3daa-81f7-4919e2e7e43b",
                                "text": "There was also the Dublin University VAD, or Voluntary Aid Detachment branch of Dublin University Women graduates and undergraduates."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fcf12315-fc28-4c4d-a7c8-9340f9e10f79",
                                "sense_id": "22bbce3a-25a3-3daa-81f7-4919e2e7e43b",
                                "text": "2008, Celia M. Kingsbury, Chapter 2: Food Will Win the War, Kathleen LeBesco, Peter Naccarato (editors), Edible Ideologies: Representing Food and Meaning, State University of New York Press, 46,\nSmith, pseudonym for freelance writer Evadne Price, obtained the war journal of a V.A.D. by the name of Winifred Young, who had turned over the diary with the stipulation that Price remain faithful to the tone."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
